# SaviorOS firmware allowlist (DESIGN 13.2), relative to the linux-firmware
# tree. Used twice:
#   * package/savior-firmware installs exactly these files from the
#     linux-firmware release Buildroot pins (install-firmware.sh);
#   * post-build.sh deletes anything else found in /lib/firmware (other
#     packages' firmware), keeping wireless-regdb's regulatory.db.
#
# Syntax: one shell glob per line ("*" also matches "/"); "#" comments.
#   pattern    must match at least one file or WHENCE "Link:" name
#   ?pattern   optional: may match nothing (files upstream may drop or move)
#   !pattern   exclude matches of the earlier patterns
# Old names are fine: when upstream moves a file and leaves a WHENCE link
# behind (e.g. iwlwifi-*.ucode -> intel/iwlwifi/...), the link is recreated
# and its target installed.
#
# Deliberately absent: amdgpu, NVIDIA GSP, and anything for hardware newer
# than this project targets. ipw2x00 and b43 firmware can't be redistributed:
# users drop it into /firmware/ on the stick. ar3k (Atheros *Bluetooth*) is
# not shipped either: SaviorOS has no Bluetooth stack. Beyond the DESIGN 13.2
# list, rtlwifi 8192c and brcmsmac firmware are included because DESIGN 14
# requires the rtl8192ce and brcmsmac drivers, which are useless without it.

# --- Intel wired: e100 microcode
e100/*

# --- Intel Wi-Fi: iwlegacy (3945, 4965), iwlwifi dvm (1000-6000 series),
# iwlwifi mvm 7260/7265/3160/3168. Only the newest API each kernel uses.
iwlwifi-3945-2.ucode
iwlwifi-4965-2.ucode
iwlwifi-1000-5.ucode
iwlwifi-100-5.ucode
iwlwifi-105-6.ucode
iwlwifi-135-6.ucode
iwlwifi-2000-6.ucode
iwlwifi-2030-6.ucode
iwlwifi-5000-5.ucode
iwlwifi-5150-2.ucode
iwlwifi-6000-4.ucode
iwlwifi-6000g2a-6.ucode
iwlwifi-6000g2b-6.ucode
iwlwifi-6050-5.ucode
iwlwifi-3160-17.ucode
iwlwifi-3168-29.ucode
iwlwifi-7260-17.ucode
iwlwifi-7265-17.ucode
iwlwifi-7265D-29.ucode

# --- Realtek wired (r8169 family)
rtl_nic/*

# --- Realtek Wi-Fi: rtl8192ce / rtl8192cu (rtl8187 needs none)
rtlwifi/rtl8192c*fw*.bin

# --- Atheros USB Wi-Fi: carl9170 (AR9170), ath9k_htc (AR9271, AR7010)
carl9170-1.fw
?ar9170*.fw
ath9k_htc/htc_9271-1.4.0.fw
ath9k_htc/htc_7010-1.4.0.fw

# --- Ralink rt2x00 (rt61pci, rt73usb, rt2800pci, rt2800usb)
rt2561.bin
rt2561s.bin
rt2661.bin
rt73.bin
rt2860.bin
rt2870.bin
rt3070.bin
?rt3071.bin
rt3090.bin
?rt3290.bin

# --- Broadcom brcmsmac (BCM4313, BCM43224, BCM43225)
brcm/bcm43xx-0.fw
brcm/bcm43xx_hdr-0.fw

# --- AMD/ATI radeon, R100 to Southern Islands. Not CIK (radeon's GCN parts
# are amdgpu territory) and no video decode/encode engines.
radeon/*
!radeon/[Bb][Oo][Nn][Aa][Ii][Rr][Ee]*
!radeon/[Hh][Aa][Ww][Aa][Ii][Ii]*
!radeon/[Kk][Aa][Vv][Ee][Rr][Ii]*
!radeon/[Kk][Aa][Bb][Ii][Nn][Ii]*
!radeon/[Mm][Uu][Ll][Ll][Ii][Nn][Ss]*
!radeon/*_uvd.bin
!radeon/*_vce.bin
